### Summary

| Area | Before | After |
|------|--------|-------|
| Click binding | `handleSelectWorkspaceApp(app)` | `handleSelectWorkspaceApp(app, $event)` |
| Handler | Always `$ui.openWorkspace(app)` | Branches on `ctrlKey \|\| metaKey` |
| New window | — | `$ui.openNewWindowAppPanel(app)` (existing store action: `${origin}${app.path}` + `window.open(url, app.name)`) |

Notes:
- **`metaKey`** covers `Cmd+Click` on macOS (where `Ctrl+Click` is the context menu).
- **`app.path` guard** — the store action builds `${origin}${app.path}`; without a guard a pathless app would navigate to `http://host/undefined`.
- **Named window** (`app.name`) means repeated Ctrl+Clicks on the same app focus the existing window instead of spawning duplicates — same behaviour as `AppBar.vue` / `WorkspacesMenu.vue`.
- No store or config changes needed.

### Accessibility note

`Ctrl+Click` is a pointer‑only, non‑discoverable affordance and is intentionally **not** the only way to get a new window — `WorkspacesMenu.vue` and the `AppIcon` menu still expose an explicit "open in new window" button for keyboard users. If you want the gesture to be discoverable in the sidebar, the cheapest addition is:

```vue
:title="isCollapsed ? app.name : `${app.name} — Ctrl+Click to open in a new window`"
```

